Shanling Q2 tools
=================

The Q2 runs Linux 5.10 on an Ingenic X2000 (MIPS32r2, nan2008) with glibc 2.28, no IPv6 and no CA
bundle. q2-deezer runs from the card's .deezer folder as a Q2 Pod card app (q2-pod's patch/addon.c):
Q2 Pod lists it in Streaming, starts it from that row, draws its page and keeps the Q2 awake while
it downloads. Nothing is flashed for it.

  build.sh     static Go for the Q2 and the card files, in target/shanlingq2/.deezer, zipped as
               target/shanlingq2/q2-deezer-vX.Y-SHA.zip (unzip that at the card's root)
  package.py   checks the binary (static, MIPS32 little-endian, soft-float ABI), sets the nan2008
               ELF flag the Q2's kernel requires and Go doesn't, and writes the ZIP
  launcher.sh  installed as .deezer/run: q2-deezer copied to /tmp and run there in a restart loop
  q2app        installed as .deezer/q2app: the card app manifest (name=Deezer, search=Search Deezer)
  icon.png, icon-40.png
               installed beside it: Streaming's row icon, 52 px (Legacy) and 40 px (iPod), Deezer's
               heart in white on Deezer purple, in Q2 Pod's style
  test_launcher.py
               runs launcher.sh on the host with a fake app

Install
-------

Q2 Pod's System settings -> Apps installs the latest release over Wi-Fi. By hand, unzip
q2-deezer-*.zip from https://github.com/group-a-study/q2-deezer/releases/latest to the card's root
with the Q2 powered off. See the top-level README.md.

Build
-----

  contrib/shanlingq2/build.sh [OUT]

Go 1.22 or later and python3. The binary is CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=mipsle GOMIPS=softfloat,
static, so it needs none of the Q2's libraries and the firmware's -mfp64 doesn't matter. The
dependencies are vendored: golang.org/x/crypto/blowfish for the decryption, and OpenDeezer's taggers
github.com/bogem/id3v2/v2 (with golang.org/x/text's encodings) and github.com/go-flac (go-flac,
flacvorbis, flacpicture). Tests: go test ./... (a fake Deezer behind the HTTP transport) and
python3 contrib/shanlingq2/test_launcher.py. A tag q2-vX.Y matching cmd/q2-deezer/main.go's version
publishes the release (.github/workflows/release.yml); System settings -> Apps takes its only ZIP.

Device
------

Q2 Pod runs /bin/sh /mnt/mmc/.deezer/run when Streaming's Deezer row is pressed and it isn't
running. The launcher copies q2-deezer and itself to /tmp and leaves the card at once, so USB storage
can always take the card; the loop restarts it after a failure, waiting 5 s and doubling to a
minute, runs it at nice 10 (playback and the Q2's pages first), and leaves its pid in /tmp/q2-deezer.
A TERM to it ends q2-deezer cleanly: the song under way is dropped (its .part removed) and the
queue saved. Q2 Pod sends it for Stop Streaming Services, Home's Rockbox row, an Apps update or
remove, and USB storage (after which it starts it again). With nothing to download and its page
unused for 15 minutes, q2-deezer stops by itself; a stream session waiting for the Q2 to play on
keeps it going (for an hour without the Q2 moving on).

  /tmp/q2-deezer.state
      hold=1 while a song downloads or streams in (Q2 Pod holds standby off) and version; while not signed in
      with a paid plan, also the sign-in page's addr, pin, qr, qrsize and note, for Q2 Pod's QR code
      page
  /tmp/q2-deezer.sock
      datagrams: q quits
  /tmp/q2-deezer.browse.sock
      Q2SPOT/1 (q2-pod's docs/librespot.md) for the Q2's page, below
  /tmp/q2-deezer.play, /tmp/q2-deezer.playing
      Stream mode (below): "<seq> <folder>", the session Q2 Pod plays; and the path of the song it
      plays from it, which Q2 Pod writes
  port 8090 (the next free one if taken)
      the sign-in page: /?k=KEY signs a browser in (the key is the QR code's, new each start),
      POST /api/login takes the PIN, POST /api/arl checks and saves an arl, POST /api/signout
      removes it; posts need the header X-Q2: 1
  .deezer/arl, .deezer/quality, .deezer/organize, .deezer/mode, .deezer/queue.json
      the sign-in, Quality (flac, mp3_320, mp3_128), Organize Files (on, off), Mode (download,
      stream) and the songs waiting; updates keep them
  .deezer/layout
      year-first once v3.2's album folders were renamed (Downloads)
  .deezer/stream/<seq>/
      Stream mode's songs, none kept past the next session

The arl is the account's sign-in: treat it like a password. One line in .deezer/arl, put there by
hand, works too. An arl lasts months; when Deezer stops taking it, the page asks to sign in again. A
Deezer outage is told apart from an expired arl (the client's ErrNoNetwork and ErrARLExpired), so a
dropped Wi-Fi never asks for a new one.

HTTPS is checked against Mozilla's CA bundle, which the app carries (internal/tlsroots, from curl's
conversion); the firmware has none. On a Q2 whose clock was never set, certificates are checked at
the time a plain HTTP Date header gives.

The page
--------

Each row's kind says what a press does (q2-pod's patch/addon.c): list opens a level, action sends an
op and toasts its reply, search opens the Q2's keyboard, remote opens the QR code, local plays from
the card (a song: its folder from it; a folder ending /: its songs listed; context album: in track
order), info does nothing. A row's position is the op Play/Pause held sends.

  menu
      Downloaded Songs, Liked Songs, Playlists, Albums, Artists, Search Deezer, Downloads, Mode,
      Quality, Organize Files, Account, Stop Deezer; signed out, Sign In from Your Phone. From the
      sign-in as last found (it never waits on Deezer); refresh
  playlists, albums, artists
      list rows: tracks <list> (Play/Pause held: download <list>), or artist <id>
  artist <id>
      Top Songs, Artist Mix, the albums, the similar artists
  tracks <list>
      Download All (or All on the card; in Stream mode Play All, stream <list>, first), then each
      song: local when on the card, else download <list>#<id>, or in Stream mode stream
      <list>#<id> (Play/Pause held still downloads); refresh
  search <term>, found <kind>:<term>
      the four kinds of one search (OpenDeezer's Search), kept two minutes
  download <list> or <list>#<id>
      queues the list's songs not on the card (or that one); its message says how many
  stream <list> or <list>#<id>
      plays the list from its first song (or that one) in a new stream session
  downloads
      the queue; cancel <id>, cancelall, retry [<id>], clearfailed
  cardartists, cardalbums <artist>
      Downloaded Songs with Artist/Album folders on the card: the songs in Deezer/ itself
      (Unsorted Songs), then each artist's folder; an artist's albums, oldest first, each a local
      folder row with context album
  mode, quality, organize, account, signout, stop
      Mode download or stream; the next Quality; Organize Files on or off; the account and Sign
      Out; the arl removed; the app stopped

Lists of songs are named liked, flow, chart, playlist:<id>, album:<id>, artistmix:<id>,
artisttop:<id> and search:<term>; they are fetched whole (OpenDeezer's paging) and kept two minutes,
so a download takes the songs as the page showed them. Cursors are offsets, read from a request's
last argument: Q2 Pod up to 1.4.1 sent each More… with the cursors of the pages before it too
("albums 30 60"), which read from the first showed the second page again. A request waits at most
8 s for its list (Q2 Pod waits 15 s): a list still coming (a 2,320-song playlist is 12 of Deezer's
pages) answers one info row, Loading..., with the message refresh, so the page asks again every 2 s
while the one fetch carries on; a list past its two minutes is shown as kept while it is fetched
again. At most two fetches run at once. The account's albums, playlists and artists come from
deezer.pageProfile, which sends the whole tab whatever nb and index ask: one request, asked again
only while short of the tab's total and still bringing new items.

Downloads
---------

As OpenDeezer's SaveTrack: for each song the client asks the gateway for its token and the media
service for its file in the best format at or below Quality that the account has (BF_CBC_STRIPE:
every third 2048-byte chunk Blowfish-CBC encrypted with a key from the track's id). Deezer licenses
music per country (the account's, which its sign-in names: an account made in Turkey is TR wherever
it is used), and some releases aren't licensed in every one: Angus & Julia Stone's Snow, album
952190521, is licensed only in Australia and New Zealand. For such a song the gateway names the
same song on another release (FALLBACK: Snow's international edition, album 48029042), which is
fetched instead, as deemix and Deezer's own apps do; its audio is decrypted with its own id, and the
file keeps the song's own name and tags. A song with neither fails, "not licensed in your Deezer
country (TR)". The file is
fetched to a temporary <name>-<n>.flac.part beside its name (a dropped connection resumed with an
HTTP range and If-Range, a CDN address that expires mid-file resolved again, a file short of its
length refused), decrypted as it arrives, tagged, then renamed into place. The tags include the song's lyrics:
LRCLIB's time-synced ones when it has them, found as Q2 Pod's own lyrics search finds them (its
search by title and first artist, the first result with synced lyrics, less opening credit lines;
asked up to 3 times, 2 s apart, while it answers busy), else Deezer's (song.getLyrics), whose lines
start about 0.75 s before they are sung. Time-synced ones are LRC, "[01:03.01]A line" a line, else
the plain text, in a FLAC's LYRICS and an MP3's USLT (UTF-8, language XXX), both of
which TagLib reads as LYRICS: Q2 Pod shows them in Now Playing (in time from 1.4.2, group-a-study's
fork), as do Navidrome and most players. One song downloads at a
time. Offline, signed out or with the card away, the queue waits and tries again every 30 s.

Organize Files on (the default, .deezer/organize missing or anything but "off"): before a song
downloads, the public API is asked where it sits (/track/<id>: its album, disc and number) and,
once per album, the album's artist, title and year (/album/<id>) and its discs (/album/<id>/tracks).
The song goes in Deezer/<album artist>/<year> - <album>/ as "07 - Title [id].flac" (the year first,
so an artist's albums sort oldest first wherever they are listed by name; an album without a year,
its title alone): "2-07 - ..." on an album
of more than one disc, three digits on an album of 100 tracks or more, so a folder's names sort in
track order. Names are cut to 180 bytes and folders to 100, and the characters a FAT card refuses
(< > : " / \ | ? * and control characters, a trailing dot or space) are replaced. The tags gain the
number, the disc (on albums of more than one) and the album artist, so the Q2's Library orders the
album too. A lookup that fails but for the network files the song by what it has (its artist and
album; no number); a failed download removes the folders it made, when empty. Navidrome, Plex and
Jellyfin group by the tags (album, album artist, date), so the folders' names don't matter to them.

v3.2 named album folders "<album> (<year>)", v3.1 "<album>". At its first start q2-deezer v3.3
renames each v3.2 folder to "<year> - <album>" (one whose new name is taken is left), then writes
.deezer/layout so it never does again; a v3.1 one, whose year only a lookup knows, is renamed when
its album's next song downloads, as is a v3.2 one left over. Library -> Update Local Music then
finds the songs at their new paths.

Organize Files off: every song in Deezer/ itself as "Title - Artist [id].flac", OpenDeezer's name.

Either way the [id] at the end of a name is how q2-deezer knows a song is on the card: it reads
Deezer/ and the folders under it (hidden ones skipped) at its start, and again when the page asks
for a list a minute or more after the last read, so songs downloaded either way, or moved by hand
within Deezer/, are found. Downloaded Songs lists an artist's albums oldest first, each by its
title with its year beside.

Stream mode
-----------

Mode: Stream (.deezer/mode "stream"; Download is the default): a press on a song plays it and the
rest of its list after it, Play All the list from its start, and nothing is kept in Deezer/. It
needs a Q2 Pod with stream support (group-a-study/q2-pod 1.4.2 or later), which plays what the app
names. A session is a folder, .deezer/stream/<seq>/ (seq: the start's time in ms), holding the
list's songs from the pressed one, at most 200, named in play order ("01 - Title [id].flac",
three digits for 100 or more), each fetched, decrypted and tagged as a download is (a song already
downloaded is copied from Deezer/ instead). /tmp/q2-deezer.play names the session, "<seq> <folder>".
Q2 Pod plays the folder from its first song once one is there, adds each later song to the end of
that queue as it comes (as Add to Queue), and writes the path of the song playing to
/tmp/q2-deezer.playing. The session fetches up to two songs past that one (past the first, before
the Q2 plays any), then waits for the Q2 to move on, deleting songs more than five before the one
playing; it ends after an hour without the Q2 moving on. A new session (another press) first moves
in the old sessions' songs it needs, renamed, and deletes the old ones. A song Deezer won't send is
left out; one that fails for the network is tried again (every 5 s, up to five times). .deezer is
a hidden folder, which Q2 Pod's library scan skips, so streamed songs never join the Library.

A song Deezer won't give the account in full (only its 30-second preview) fails, as OpenDeezer
refuses to save a preview under a full song's name. The song under way is counted in queue.json
before it starts and the count taken back when it returns, so only a death of q2-deezer under way
(killed, out of memory, a crash) leaves it counted: one counted three times goes to the failed
songs ("it stopped Deezer each time") instead of first again after every restart. The temp files an
interrupted download left are swept when q2-deezer starts.

The client
----------

internal/deezer is OpenDeezer's internal/deezer, so it can be brought up to date by copying
OpenDeezer's files over it, with these differences:

  q2.go        the additions: UseTransport (every request, the CDN's and the cover's included,
               through the app's TLS roots), FavoriteAlbums and FavoriteArtists, AlbumInfo,
               SaveTrackInfo and SaveTrackInfoAs (SaveTrack for a song already looked up, the
               latter with its file's name given), TrackPlacement, OrganizedName and FolderName
  models.go    Track's DiscNumber and AlbumArtist, which Organize Files fills in, and Lyrics (LyricsTag)
  tags.go      a FLAC is tagged without holding its audio: only the metadata blocks are read and the
               audio copied across (OpenDeezer's ParseFile and Marshal built the whole file in
               memory, which ran the Q2, without swap, out of memory); DISCNUMBER/TPOS and
               ALBUMARTIST/TPE2 when known; LYRICS/USLT
  download.go  a FLAC's temporary file keeps its extension (<name>-*.flac.part), as tagFile goes by
               it; saveTrackAs, saveTrack with the file's name given
  client.go    no PrepareStreamCached (nothing streams here); its HTTP client on UseTransport's;
               the account's COUNTRY (Country); PrepareStream follows song.getData's FALLBACK
               when the song itself isn't licensed for the account

OpenDeezer's internal/log is internal/log, writing to the app's log in /tmp (debug lines only with
Q2_DEBUG set). The rest (podcasts, playlist editing, ISRC lookup, the batch SaveAlbum and
SavePlaylist) is there, unused.
